[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125417,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dermal melanoma is a primary melanoma limited to the dermis and subcutis, without intraepidermal involvement, regression, or ulceration.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125418,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8750/3 Dermal melanoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125419,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C30.Y Other specified melanoma of skin</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125420,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125421,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125422,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is no specific localization {11074704}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125423,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dermal melanoma manifests as a solitary firm nodule of variable size, most often &lt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;mm, with variable colour, ranging from flesh-coloured to red to blue {14732666}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125424,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dermal melanomas are rare tumours, accounting for &lt;&nbsp;1% of all melanomas {11074704}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125425,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125426,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The pathogenesis is not fully understood. Dermal melanomas with <em>BRAF</em> and <em>NRAS</em> driver mutations have a similar oncogenic progression to that of other melanomas with these anomalies {27846954; 32946880}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125427,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125428,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "<p>Dermal melanoma is a circumscribed dermal, or dermal to subcutaneous nodule composed of atypical melanocytes {18209168; 11074704}. Tumours may display areas of necrosis and haemorrhage {14732666}. Cytomorphology may be epithelioid, spindled, rhabdoid, or pleomorphic, and mitoses are common.</p>\r\n<p>By definition, ulceration or significant regression, having possibly obliterated an intraepidermal component, should not be present {14732666; 18209168}. A precursor naevus excludes this diagnosis.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Neoplastic melanocytes express melanocytic markers, including melan-A, SOX10, HMB45, and S100 {32946880}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>Metastatic melanoma is typically associated with a history of melanoma, clinically suspected melanoma elsewhere, or multiple lesions of rapid growth. Local recurrence of melanoma typically shows an adjacent scar. A regressed intraepidermal component of a conventional melanoma is indicated by papillary dermal fibrosis, often with melanophages.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:30:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125429,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125430,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mutations in <em>GNAQ</em> or <em>GNA11</em> suggest melanoma arising in blue naevus. Fusions in relevant genes suggest mesenchymal tumours such as cutaneous clear cell sarcoma {20087159} or a cutaneous tumour with <em>CRTC1</em>::<em>TRIM11</em> rearrangement.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125431,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a melanoma confined to the dermis and subcutis without an intraepidermal component, ulceration, or regression; absence of prior history of melanoma and exclusion of melanoma at another site.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125432,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dermal melanoma is staged according to the American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) TNM criteria like other cutaneous melanomas {29028110}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125433,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The prognosis is better than for metastatic melanoma and better than for other melanomas of similar thickness. However, locoregional recurrences, distant metastases, and deaths have been reported {11074704; 14732666; 18209168}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]